      {
        "turn": 6,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Great, that takes some pressure off! Back to home repairs\u2014if I do get a chain and need to open it, how do I actually use a chain breaker tool?",
          "user_rubrik": "How do I use a chain breaker to open my bike chain?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To use a chain breaker tool, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Position the Chain**: Place the chain in the tool so that the pin you want to push out is aligned with the tool's pin pusher.\n\n2. **Adjust the Tool**: Make sure the chain is securely held in place, and adjust the tool so that the pusher is just touching the pin.\n\n3. **Push the Pin**: Turn the handle or knob of the tool to push the pin out. Go slowly and ensure that the pin is coming out straight. If it feels stuck, stop and check to avoid damaging the chain.\n\n4. **Remove the Chain Link**: Once the pin is pushed out, you can separate the chain links. If you're connecting a new chain, align the links and insert a new pin.\n\n5. **Reassemble**: If you're reattaching the chain, ensure that the new pin is inserted correctly and secure it by pushing it back into place with the tool.\n\nAlways refer to the specific instructions that come with your chain breaker tool, as designs may vary slightly.",
          "citations": {
