    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 7,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks, I think I get it\u2014might take some practice! So, what should I use to lubricate a bike chain?",
          "user_rubrik": "What should I use to lubricate a bike chain?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To lubricate your bike chain, you have several good options depending on your riding conditions. For dry and dusty environments, the Muc Off Dry Lube is a great choice as it uses a wax-based formula that repels contaminants and is biodegradable. If you're looking for a budget-friendly option, the White Lightning Epic Ride Bicycle Chain Lubricant works well in both moist and dry conditions, providing protection for up to 100 miles. For a more versatile lubricant that performs in various conditions, the Park Tool CL-1 Synthetic Blend Bicycle Chain Lube, which contains PTFE, is ideal as it helps reduce noise and extends the life of your drivetrain. Make sure to apply the lubricant to a clean and dry chain for the best results.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0011-31-03597:6": 0.217376708984375
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      }
    ],
