      {
        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I\u2019m actually trying to figure out why my bike chain keeps derailing. Any ideas?",
          "user_rubrik": "Why does my bike chain keep derailing?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "It sounds like your bike chain might be derailing due to a few common issues. First, check if your derailleur is properly aligned and not bent, as misalignment can cause the chain to slip off. Also, inspect the chain for wear or damage, as an old or stretched chain can derail more easily. Another potential cause could be improper chain tension or a mismatch between the chain and cassette. Since you mentioned you're not very handy with DIY, it might be a good idea to take your bike to a local shop for a quick tune-up. They can adjust the derailleur, check the chain length, and ensure everything is in good working order. Given the hilly terrain in your area, maintaining your bike\u2019s drivetrain is especially important for smooth rides.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0018-47-10956:0": 20.222400665283203,
            "clueweb22-en0002-21-11444:10": 17.976200103759766,
