    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "My bike chain keeps derailing\u2014do you know what might cause that?",
          "user_rubrik": "Why does my bike chain keep derailing?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Common causes for a bike chain derailing include misaligned or poorly adjusted derailleurs, especially after a crash or rough use, as well as worn or damaged cassette (rear gears) or chainrings (front gears) [clueweb22-en0020-44-10600]. If the chain or gears are bent, broken, or excessively worn, the chain may not stay in place. Incorrect chain routing through the derailleur or improper adjustment of the limit screws can also cause the chain to slip off [clueweb22-en0008-26-01793]. It's important to inspect the chain, derailleurs, and gears for visible damage and ensure everything is properly aligned and adjusted. Sometimes, easing off pedaling while shifting and avoiding putting too much load on the chain when it's not fully in gear can help prevent derailment [clueweb22-en0005-72-07512]. Are you interested in beginner-friendly tools for simple bike repairs?",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0005-72-07512:3": 0.047712258380229994,
