            "I have a small garage that I use as workshop space at home."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 6,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks, that\u2019s clear! Now, about lube: what should I use to lubricate a bike chain?",
          "user_rubrik": "What should I use to lubricate a bike chain?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Since you ride in rainy weather and forested areas, a wet chain lube like WD-40 Specialist Bike Wet Chain Lube is ideal\u2014it forms a durable, water-repellent coating that protects your chain from mud and moisture without building up grime. For dry, dusty days, a dry lube such as Muc Off Dry Lube is better, as it won't attract dust and keeps your chain running smoothly. There are also all-conditions lubes and eco-friendly options available; look for products labeled as biodegradable or plant-based if sustainability is important to you. Always clean and dry your chain before applying any lube, and avoid using general-purpose grease, as it attracts too much dirt. Apply the lube sparingly, wipe off excess, and reapply regularly based on your riding conditions for best results [clueweb22-en0011-31-03597:4][clueweb22-en0026-21-09546:2][clueweb22-en0011-31-03597:8].",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0011-31-03597:4": 0.06412491980514422,
            "clueweb22-en0011-31-03597:8": 0.06359921024962364,
            "clueweb22-en0026-21-09546:2": 0.06204838900734423,
            "clueweb22-en0026-21-09546:1": 0.053580307138099574
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": [
            "I like biking even in rainy weather and in the forest.",
            "I care about sustainability and avoiding waste.",
            "I am not really handy with DIY."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 7,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Great, thanks! When should I add grease on a bike chain?",
          "user_rubrik": "When should I add grease on a bike chain? ",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Grease is too thick for bike chains and can attract excessive dirt and debris, leading to poor performance and increased wear. Instead, use a specific bike chain lubricant\u2014wet lube for rainy or muddy conditions, and dry lube for dry, dusty rides. Apply lube after thoroughly cleaning and drying your chain, especially after riding in wet, muddy, or gritty conditions, or if the chain starts to sound dry or squeaky. Wipe off any excess lube to prevent buildup. Regular lubrication helps extend the life of your chain and drivetrain [clueweb22-en0011-31-03597:4][clueweb22-en0026-21-09546:2]. What are the signs that my chain needs lubrication?",
          "citations": {
