    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Actually, I\u2019d like a step-by-step for using a chain breaker to open my chain. Could you give me that?",
          "user_rubrik": "How do I use a chain breaker to open my bike chain?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "A chain breaker is a simple tool that lets you remove your bike chain by pushing out one of its pins. Here\u2019s a step-by-step guide: (1) Place your bike on a stable surface. (2) Position the chain in the slot of the chain breaker tool, making sure the tool\u2019s driving pin lines up with a chain pin you want to remove. (3) Slowly turn the handle of the tool to push the chain pin out\u2014go slowly to avoid pushing the pin all the way through unless you\u2019re removing the chain completely. (4) Once the pin is almost out, you can wiggle the chain to separate the links. Some chain breakers also help you reinsert the pin or install a quick link for reassembly. Tools like the Oumers Universal Bike Chain Tool are designed for easy operation and are beginner-friendly, making them a good choice if you\u2019re not very handy with DIY [clueweb22-en0010-59-02845:0][clueweb22-en0038-96-11763:1].",
