    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 4,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "A quick overview of the steps would be great! Also: how do I use a chain breaker to open my bike chain?",
          "user_rubrik": "How do I use a chain breaker to open my bike chain?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For a quick overview: (1) Thread the new chain around your largest front chainring and largest rear cog (not through the derailleur), pull the ends together, and add two extra links for proper length. (2) If the chain is too long, use a chain breaker tool: place the chain in the tool, align the pin with the tool's driving pin, and turn the handle to push the chain pin out, separating the chain at the desired link. (3) Reconnect the chain using a quick link or by pressing the pin back in, then check tension and shifting. Chain breaker tools are designed to be easy to use\u2014just make sure the tool is lined up with the chain pin, and apply steady pressure to push the pin out. Some tools have replaceable pins for durability, and you don't need to file the rivet heads. If you're unsure or not confident, a bike shop can help with the process [clueweb22-en0010-22-02970][clueweb22-en0020-78-15858].",
