      {
        "turn": 7,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That helps, thanks! I actually thought I should be using grease sometimes, so good to know. For chain cleaning and lubing\u2014does rain or muddy riding mean I should do it more often?",
          "user_rubrik": "When should I add grease on a bike chain? ",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Wet and muddy conditions introduce grit, water, and debris that can quickly wear down your chain and wash away lubricant. Experts recommend cleaning and lubricating your chain after every ride in the rain or mud to prevent rust, corrosion, and excess wear. This involves rinsing off mud, drying the chain thoroughly, and applying fresh wet lube, then wiping away any excess. In dry conditions, you can clean and lube your chain once a week or every few weeks, but wet weather requires much more frequent attention to keep your drivetrain running smoothly and to extend its lifespan [clueweb22-en0042-05-05603][clueweb22-en0018-88-19973][clueweb22-en0001-67-10868]. Are there eco-friendly degreasers or lubes you\u2019d like to try?",
