        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Why does my bike chain keep derailing?",
          "user_rubrik": "Why does my bike chain keep derailing?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Your bike chain keeps derailing mainly due to three common, fixable issues:\n\n**1. Chain Wear and Stretch**\n- Chains stretch and wear out over time, especially if not replaced regularly. A stretched chain won\u2019t fit snugly on the gears, causing it to slip or derail\u2014this is especially likely if you ride in rough, hilly, or wet conditions like you described.\n\n**2. Cable Tension Problems**\n- Gear cables stretch with use, leading to poor shifting and chain skipping. This is a frequent issue after moving to hillier terrain or if your bike hasn\u2019t been tuned recently.\n\n**3. Chain Length or Derailleur Adjustment**\n- If the chain is too long or the derailleur isn\u2019t adjusted correctly, the chain can jump off, especially on bumpy paths.\n\n**What fits your preferences:**\n- Since you value comfort and prefer upgrades over replacements, start with a professional tune-up: ask for cable tension adjustment and a chain wear check. This is a quick, affordable service and doesn\u2019t require DIY skills.\n- If your chain is only slightly worn,",
          "citations": {
