      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "What about the best way to maintain a bike chain?",
          "user_rubrik": "What is the perfect length of a chain for a bike?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 0,
          "text": "The best way to maintain your bike chain\u2014especially as a casual rider who values comfort, reliability, and sustainability\u2014is to focus on regular, simple cleaning and proper lubrication using the right products. This approach upgrades your ride quality, extends chain life, and avoids unnecessary replacements.\n\n**Essentials for Easy, Effective Chain Maintenance:**\n\n- **Clean Monthly (or More Often in Rain/Mud):**\n  - Wipe the chain with a damp rag to remove dirt.\n  - For heavy grime, use a basic degreaser and an old toothbrush.\n  - No need for special tools or deep disassembly\u2014your bike shop can do a thorough clean if you prefer.\n\n- **Lubricate with Bike-Specific Lube:**\n  - Use a mineral-based lubricant made for bikes\u2014not household oils or sprays, which can damage the chain.\n  - For wet weather, choose a \"wet lube\" (sticks better in rain/forest conditions).\n  - Apply a drop to each link, wipe off excess to prevent dirt build-up.\n\n- **Check for Wear:**\n  - Ask your",
