          "user_utterance": "How often should I apply lubricant to the chain?",
          "user_rubrik": "When should I add grease on a bike chain? ",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For your casual, comfort-focused riding in wet, hilly, and forested conditions, apply **wet bike chain lubricant** about **once a month**\u2014or more often if you ride frequently in rain or mud.\n\n**Key points tailored to you:**\n- **Wet lube** is best for your environment: it resists being washed off by rain and mud, protects against rust, and reduces noise (clueweb22-en0042-05-05603, clueweb22-en0011-31-03597).\n- **Monthly application** is ideal for most casual riders (clueweb22-en0024-04-10077, clueweb22-en0042-05-05603). If your chain gets noisy, gritty, or you ride in especially harsh conditions, reapply sooner.\n- **Always clean the chain first**\u2014wipe off dirt and old lube before applying new (clueweb22-en0026-21-09546).\n\nThis routine keeps your bike running smoothly, extends chain life, and avoids unnecessary waste\u2014no technical skills required.",
