      {
        "turn": 7,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks for the steps. By the way, what kind of lube should I use on the new chain? There are so many types\u2014any clue which is best for mixed weather and forest trails?",
          "user_rubrik": "What should I use to lubricate a bike chain?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For mixed weather and forest trails, a wet chain lube would be a good choice. It's designed to stay on the chain in wet conditions and protect it from mud and water. Look for a biodegradable and water-resistant lube that won't attract dirt or dust. You can also consider a dry lube for dry conditions, but a wet lube will provide better protection in mixed weather. Apply the lube according to the manufacturer's instructions and wipe off any excess to prevent attracting dirt. Regular lubrication will help keep your chain running smoothly and prolong its lifespan.",
