          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Great, thanks! Do you know how often I should clean and reapply bike lube? Is too much lube bad?",
          "user_rubrik": "When should I add grease on a bike chain? ",
          "user_rubrik_score": 4,
          "text": "You should clean and reapply bike lube regularly, ideally every 1-2 weeks or after riding in wet conditions. Too much lube can be bad, as it attracts dirt and dust, which can compromise your bike's performance. It's essential to wipe away excess lube after application to prevent this. Regular cleaning and lubrication will help keep your chain running smoothly and prolong its lifespan. If you ride your bike daily, you may need to clean and lube it more frequently, such as once a week. However, if you don't ride as often, you can clean and lube it every 2 weeks.",
