          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To use a chain breaker tool, you'll need to locate the special connecting rivet on your chain and avoid breaking it there. Then, place the chain in the tool and tighten it until the pin pushes the rivet out. It's a two-step process that holds the chain link and applies force to the center to quickly remove the pin. Some chain breaker tools also come with an adjustable feature, allowing you to cut the chain to the desired length without needing other equipment. Make sure to choose a tool that fits your chain size to avoid any mistakes. It's a relatively simple process, but if you're not comfortable with it, you can always consult your bike's manual or visit a local bike shop for guidance.",
