          "user_rubrik": "What should I use to lubricate a bike chain?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For rainy weather or forest riding, you'll want to use a wet lube. It's thicker and more water-resistant, so it won't get washed away by water or mud. Wet lubes are ideal for wet conditions and can provide long-lasting protection for your chain. On the other hand, dry lubes are better suited for dry and dusty conditions. They attract less dirt and are less messy, but may need to be reapplied more frequently. Consider using a wet lube for your forest rides and switching to a dry lube for drier conditions. Always clean your chain before applying lube to ensure the best results.",
