          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s still not really answering why the chain comes off. I\u2019m not super handy, so could you explain what causes it in simple terms? Is it something about the derailleur or the gears?",
          "user_rubrik": "Why does my bike chain keep derailing?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "The chain coming off is often related to the derailleur, which is a part of the bike that helps move the chain between gears. If the derailleur is not adjusted properly, it can cause the chain to jump out of gear, leading to clicking sounds and derailing. This is especially common on bumpy paths, as the derailleur can get knocked out of alignment. Additionally, worn-out components like sprockets and chainrings can also cause the chain to derail. It's possible that your bike just needs a tune-up to get everything adjusted and running smoothly again. You might want to consider taking it to a local bike shop for a professional adjustment.",
