      {
        "turn": 6,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thank you, that helps! I\u2019ve seen people use a chain breaker tool\u2014how do I actually use one to open my bike chain?",
          "user_rubrik": "How do I use a chain breaker to open my bike chain?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To use a chain breaker tool, you'll need to place the chain on the tool and position the pin on the chain link you want to break. Then, turn the handle to push the pin out of the link, effectively breaking the chain. This will allow you to remove or add links as needed to adjust the chain length. It's a relatively simple process, but if you're not comfortable with DIY tasks, it's always best to consult a professional or take your bike to a local shop for assistance. Additionally, make sure to purchase a chain breaker tool that is compatible with your bike's chain type.",
          "citations": {
