        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 8,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That clarifies things! When should I add grease on a bike chain?",
          "user_rubrik": "When should I add grease on a bike chain? ",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "You shouldn't use grease on a bike chain as it picks up too much dirt and makes a mess. Instead, use a lubricant specifically designed for bike chains, such as dry or wet lube, depending on your riding conditions. These lubricants are designed to keep your chain running smoothly and protect it from the elements. If you need to lubricate other parts of your bike, such as brake pivots or cables, you can use the same chain lubricant. However, for parts that require grease, such as bearings or bushings, use a separate grease product specifically designed for those components.",
