          "text": "For lubricating a bike chain, you should use a lubricant specifically designed for bike chains. These lubricants are usually mineral-based and contain Teflon, which helps repel dirt and water. They come in different types, such as dry and wet lubes, and some are suitable for all conditions. It's essential to choose the right type of lubricant for your riding conditions and to apply it regularly to keep your chain running smoothly. Avoid using grease or other non-bicycle-specific products, as they can attract dirt and cause problems. You can also use the same lubricant on other moving parts of your bike, like brake pivots and cables. Remember to always clean your chain before applying lubricant for optimal results.",
