    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 7,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks for the options! When should I add grease on a bike chain?",
          "user_rubrik": "When should I add grease on a bike chain? ",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "You should lube your bike chain every week, ideally after a day's riding, so the lube has time to work into the nooks and crannies. Grease is not recommended for bike chains, as it's too thick to penetrate into the internal bearing surfaces of the chain. Instead, use a chain lube that's suitable for your riding conditions. For dry conditions, a dry lube is best, while for wet conditions, a wet lube is recommended. You can also use a chain lube that's designed for both dry and wet conditions. It's also a good idea to clean your chain before applying lubricant to ensure it works effectively. Consider using a chain retention technology from mountain biking to ensure your chain stays in place. Get your bike serviced regularly to prevent such problems. Consider using a chain retention technology from mountain biking to ensure your chain stays in place. You can also try using a chain lube that's specifically designed for mountain biking, such as Dumonde Tech",
