          "user_rubrik": "How do I use a chain breaker to open my bike chain?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Using a chain breaker to open your bike chain is straightforward and fits your workshop approach. First, position your bike chain on a stable surface or mount the bike on a stand to keep it steady. Identify the pin you want to push out\u2014usually a link where you want to break the chain. Place the chain so the chain breaker\u2019s driving pin lines up directly over the chain pin. Slowly turn the handle clockwise to push the chain pin out of the link. Be careful not to push the pin all the way out unless you want to fully separate the chain; just push it enough to free the link. Once loosened, you can pull the chain apart gently. After opening, you can adjust the chain length or replace the chain. Since you prefer upgrading and have limited DIY experience, take your time and avoid forcing the tool; a smooth, controlled motion works best. Watching a detailed video tutorial before trying can also help you feel more confident.",
          "citations": {},
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      }
    ],
    "judgment": {
      "engagement": "True Collaborative Partner",
      "relevance-and-usefulness": "Highly meets",
      "overall-subtopic-quality": "Exceptional",
      "subtopic-justification": "Specific responses to user concerns",
