        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Could the chain itself be the cause of my chain dropping, even though the derailleur seems properly aligned?",
          "user_rubrik": "Could the chain itself be the cause of my chain dropping, even though the derailleur seems properly aligned?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Yes, a worn or stretched chain can definitely cause your bike chain to drop, even if your derailleur appears properly aligned. Over time, chain links elongate due to wear, causing the chain to no longer mesh snugly with the sprockets. This can lead to slipping, skipping teeth, and ultimately the chain falling off. You can measure your chain for stretch with a tool, or a bike shop can check it. If stretched or worn, replacing the chain (and often the cassette) is necessary.",
