      {
        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I actually have a question! My bike chain keeps coming off\u2014do you know what could cause that?",
          "user_rubrik": "Why does my bike chain keep derailing?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Common causes for a mountain bike chain to come off include:\n\n*   **Derailleur issues on rough terrain:** On trails, the derailleur can bounce, causing the chain to fall off. Modern mountain bike derailleurs with a \"clutch\" mechanism help prevent this by maintaining chain tension.\n*   **Improper shifting:** Shifting too many gears at once, making \"desperate\" shifts under strain (like on a steep climb), or \"crossing the chain\" (using extreme gear combinations) can dislodge it.\n*   **Derailleur adjustment:** Incorrect tension or stop screw settings on your derailleur can cause the chain to slip off.\n*   **Worn chain:** An old or stretched chain can lead to poor performance and chain drops.",
          "citations": {
