        "turn": 6,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That makes sense! When should I actually add more grease or lube to the bike chain?",
          "user_rubrik": "When should I add grease on a bike chain? ",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For your mountain bike, especially with wet lube and riding on forest trails, rough paths, and in rainy weather, you'll need to lubricate your chain more frequently.\n\nA general guideline is every 2-4 weeks or 100-200 miles. However, for extreme conditions like heavy rains or off-road riding, you should cut these intervals in half. It's also crucial to clean, dry, and re-lube your chain immediately after riding in the rain. Listen for squeaking or gritty/crunchy sounds, as these are clear indicators that your chain needs lubrication.",
