      {
        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I\u2019m actually looking for some help! My bike chain keeps derailing. Any ideas why that happens?",
          "user_rubrik": "Why does my bike chain keep derailing?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Your bike chain can derail for several reasons. Common culprits include loose or stretched derailleur cables, which affect shifting, and poorly adjusted derailleurs, including their limit screws. Worn-out components like the chain, sprockets, or chainrings can also be a factor. Less common causes include an incorrect chain length, a misaligned rear wheel, or using extreme gear combinations (cross-chaining). Since you're not handy with DIY, it's often best to have a bike mechanic check these adjustments and components.",
