          "user_utterance": "Could the chain itself be the cause of my chain dropping, even though the derailleur seems properly aligned?",
          "user_rubrik": "Could the chain itself be the cause of my chain dropping, even though the derailleur seems properly aligned?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Yes, a worn or damaged bike chain can absolutely cause derailment, even if your derailleur seems properly aligned. A stretched or worn chain won't fit snugly on the sprockets, leading to consistent slipping and the chain falling off. Worn-out components like chainrings or cassettes can also contribute, as they may not grip the chain effectively anymore.",
