          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Makes sense! If my chain is worn out and I need a new one\u2014how do I figure out what the perfect length for my bike chain is?",
          "user_rubrik": "What is the perfect length of a chain for a bike?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To determine the perfect length for a new bike chain, especially if the old one is worn, you have a few options. First, if your old chain was correctly sized, you can count its links and cut the new chain to match. A reliable alternative is the 'largest cog and largest chainring' method: wrap the new chain around the largest front chainring and largest rear cog, bypassing the derailleur. Find the closest point where the ends meet and add two full links. A calculation method using your bike's chainstay length and cog/chainring teeth is also available.",
