      {
        "turn": 4,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Oh, interesting. What if I use a chain breaker tool\u2014how do I open the chain safely with it?",
          "user_rubrik": "How do I use a chain breaker to open my bike chain?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To safely open your bike chain with a chain breaker tool, first, ensure the chain tool's prongs fit securely around a link, aligning its pin with the chain's rivet. Turn the tool's handle clockwise to push the rivet out. If you plan to reconnect the chain, do not push the rivet completely through; leave it slightly protruding. If not, you can push it all the way. Then, turn the handle counterclockwise to remove the tool and gently wiggle the link to separate the chain, being careful not to deform it.",
