      {
        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That doesn\u2019t sound too scary\u2014thanks! Once I put the new chain on, what should I use to lubricate the bike chain?",
          "user_rubrik": "What should I use to lubricate a bike chain?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For riding in rainy weather and on rough, hilly paths, a wet-specific or all-conditions lubricant is recommended. Wet lubes are designed to repel water and mud, making them durable for your conditions. Options include Muc-Off Wet Chain Lube or WD-40 Specialist Bike Wet Chain Lube. Ceramic Wet lubes, like Finish Line's, are also highly durable in wet weather and popular for mountain biking. For an environmentally friendly choice, look for biodegradable options.",
