    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 6,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s helpful. When should I add grease on a bike chain?",
          "user_rubrik": "When should I add grease on a bike chain? ",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Generally, you should not add grease to your bike chain for regular lubrication. Grease is typically too thick to penetrate the internal bearing surfaces of the chain, which are the critical areas needing lubrication. Instead, it tends to sit on the surface, attracting dirt and grime, which can increase friction and wear. While chain manufacturers may apply an initial coating of grease, for ongoing maintenance, it's recommended to use specific bike chain lubricants (oils or wax-based lubes) that can properly penetrate the links.",
