      {
        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "So how do I know what the correct length of a chain should be for my bike?",
          "user_rubrik": "What is the perfect length of a chain for a bike?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To determine the correct chain length for your mountain bike, a common method is to route the chain around the largest front chainring and largest rear cog, bypassing the rear derailleur. Then, add one full link (or two half links) to this length.\n\nAlternatively, you can calculate it by considering your chainstay length and the number of teeth on your largest front and rear sprockets. Ensure the chain isn't too tight when in the largest front/largest rear gear combination, or too slack when in the smallest front/smallest rear combination.",
