        "turn": 7,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Nice, that sounds manageable. What should I use to lubricate a bike chain after putting it back together?",
          "user_rubrik": "What should I use to lubricate a bike chain?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For lubricating your bike chain, use a lubricant specifically designed for bicycles. Avoid household sprays, vegetable oils, motor oils, general grease, and especially WD-40, as they are not suitable (P1, P2, P3, P4, P15).\n\nGiven your mountain biking on rough paths and in potentially rainy weather, a wet lube or an all-conditions lubricant is recommended (P2, P4, P9, P10, P18, P19). Wet lubes are designed to stay on in muddy and wet conditions, while all-conditions lubes offer versatility for varied weather (P10, P11).",
