      {
        "turn": 8,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "When should I add grease on a bike chain?",
          "user_rubrik": "When should I add grease on a bike chain? ",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "You generally should not add grease to a bike chain for regular lubrication. While chains come with factory grease applied during assembly, which is ideal, users should avoid applying grease themselves because it's too thick to penetrate the internal bearing surfaces where lubrication is needed. Grease also attracts excessive dirt and grime, leading to premature wear and a messy drivetrain. Instead, use a bicycle-specific chain lubricant.",
