      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Sorry, this wasn\u2019t what I was asking about. I\u2019m not looking for pedal advice right now. Can you tell me possible reasons why a bike chain would keep derailing, especially on a mountain bike?",
          "user_rubrik": "Why does my bike chain keep derailing?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Common reasons for a bike chain derailing, especially on a mountain bike, include a worn or stretched chain, misaligned or poorly adjusted derailleurs, or a bent derailleur hanger. Worn chainrings or sprockets can also be culprits. For mountain biking, a chain that's too short or snagging a stick can cause problems. Modern mountain bike derailleurs often feature a clutch mechanism to prevent derailing on rough terrain.",
