      {
        "turn": 6,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I see, thanks for breaking that down. If I need to adjust the chain length, how do I use a chain breaker to open my bike chain safely?",
          "user_rubrik": "How do I use a chain breaker to open my bike chain?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To safely open your bike chain with a chain breaker:\n1. Position a chain link in the tool's groove, aligning the pin you wish to remove with the tool's push pin.\n2. Turn the handle clockwise to push the pin.\n3. If you plan to re-use the chain, push the pin just enough for the link to separate, but not completely out of the opposite outer plate. This prevents losing the pin and aids reassembly.\n4. Once separated, the links will come apart.",
