          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I\u2019m interested in why my bike chain keeps derailing. Any ideas?",
          "user_rubrik": "Why does my bike chain keep derailing?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Common reasons for a bicycle chain to derail include loose or stretched derailleur cables, which affect shifting. Poorly adjusted derailleurs are another frequent cause, as they might not guide the chain correctly. Worn-out components like an old, stretched chain, sprockets, or chainrings can also lead to derailment. Additionally, an incorrect chain length or misaligned wheels and components can cause the chain to jump off.",
