          "user_rubrik": "Could the chain itself be the cause of my chain dropping, even though the derailleur seems properly aligned?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Yes, absolutely. Even if your derailleur seems properly aligned, a worn-out or \"stretched\" chain can be a primary cause of dropping. Over time, chains lengthen, and their links no longer fit snugly with the sprockets or chainrings. This wear prevents the chain from gripping properly, leading to slipping and derailment. Similarly, worn sprockets or chainrings themselves, with hooked or damaged teeth, can fail to hold the chain securely. In such cases, no amount of derailleur adjustment will fix the issue; component replacement is necessary.",
