      {
        "turn": 6,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s a relief! Are chains specific to the number of gears on your bike, or are they pretty universal?",
          "user_rubrik": "How do I use a chain breaker to open my bike chain?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 0,
          "text": "No, bike chains are not universal; they are specific to the number of gears, or \"speeds,\" on your bicycle. The more speeds your bike has, the narrower the chain needs to be for proper fit and function. For mountain bikes, chains are typically designed for specific speeds like 10, 11, or 12. It's essential to match the chain's speed to your bike's gear count, and for optimal compatibility, sometimes matching the brand to your drivetrain is also recommended.",
