      {
        "turn": 9,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Should I clean the chain first before applying the lube, or just add more lube on top if I\u2019m short on time?",
          "user_rubrik": "When should I add grease on a bike chain? ",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Yes, you should always clean your bike chain before applying lubricant. Lubricating a dirty chain pushes abrasive particles into the links, which significantly accelerates wear and reduces chain life.\n\nIf you're short on time and the chain only has light dust or surface grime, a quick wipe with a clean, dry rag or lint-free cloth is often sufficient to remove the visible muck. For very dirty chains, a more thorough cleaning with degreaser is necessary. Avoid simply adding lube on top of a heavily soiled chain, as this will trap abrasive particles.",
