        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "What\u2019s the ideal length for a bike chain, or does that depend on the type of bike?",
          "user_rubrik": "What is the perfect length of a chain for a bike?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 3,
          "text": "The ideal chain length for your mountain bike depends on several factors, including its chainstay length, and the number of teeth on your largest chainring and rear sprocket. One calculation method involves adding your multiplied chainstay length, divided chainring and rear sprocket teeth, plus 1 inch (2.5 cm). For mountain bikes, especially full-suspension, consider chain growth from suspension compression. If you change your chainring size by more than 2 teeth, you'll likely need to adjust your chain length. Chain width also varies based on the number of speeds.",
