      {
        "turn": 7,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s helpful, thank you! I realize I\u2019m also not clear on how to actually use a chain breaker tool to open my bike chain. Could you walk me through that process simply?",
          "user_rubrik": "How do I use a chain breaker to open my bike chain?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To use a chain breaker tool, first, locate the two prongs on the tool that fit around a chain link. Slide the link securely between these prongs, aligning the tool's small metal pin with the chain's pin. Your chain has outer plates, inner plates, rollers, and pins; you're pushing out a pin. Turn the handle clockwise to push the pin. Importantly, if you want to reuse the link or shorten the chain, do not push the pin completely out\u2014just enough so it's clear of the outer plate but still attached.",
