        "turn": 8,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That sounds doable! I might look for a video, too. Back to maintenance: What should I use to lubricate a bike chain?",
          "user_rubrik": "What should I use to lubricate a bike chain?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Given your riding conditions\u2014frequent rides in rainy weather and forests, and on hills/rough paths\u2014you should primarily use a **wet lubricant** or an **all-conditions lubricant**.\n\nWet lubes are specifically formulated to repel water and mud, providing durable protection. Examples include Muc-Off Wet Chain Lube, WD-40 Specialist Bike Wet Chain Lube, and Ceramic Wet lubes like Finish Line Ceramic Wet, known for extreme durability in wet weather and suitability for mountain biking. Thicker lubes generally last longer in rainy environments. All-conditions options like ProGold Prolink Chain Lube or Park Tool CL-1 Synthetic Blend also work well. These ensure your chain stays protected and performs smoothly.",
          "citations": {
