          "text": "Good question \u2014 useful simple cues and a practical routine:  When to reapply - After any wet ride or long exposure to rain/mud: reapply wet lube as soon as you can.   - If the chain sounds dry (squeaks, clicks) or shifting feels rough/ skips under load.   - Visibly dry-looking chain, rust spots, or gritty/dirt-caked rollers.   - Routine interval: ~100\u2013200 miles for mixed use; shorter (every ride or every few rides) in very wet/mucky conditions.  Quick routine (works in your small garage) 1. Wipe chain with a rag after every ride to remove grit.   2. Apply 1 drop per roller while backpedaling slowly. Let sit 5\u201310 min, then thoroughly wipe off excess.   3. After heavy rain, repeat even if recently lubed.   4. Prefer biodegradable wet lube for rainy/forest riding (less environmental impact).    If you notice persistent noise or skipping after lubing, check chain wear or bring photos to your shop.",
